---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/justuno-alternative';
const title = "Justuno alternatives: preserve capture before changing SMS";
const desc = "Compare the current product scope, practical replacement choices and a reversible Shopify handover for Justuno.";
const faqs = [{"question": "Should I leave because the Shopify listing is unavailable?", "answer": "Confirm your account, support and installation options directly. Listing unavailability alone does not show that Justuno has shut down."}, {"question": "Does replacing SMS replace Justuno?", "answer": "Only if the candidate also reproduces the capture, quiz, identity and destination behavior you use. A sender change alone does not establish that."}, {"question": "What must a quiz migration preserve?", "answer": "Keep typed answers, skipped values, quiz versions, identity rules and separate channel permission, then reconcile actual destination records and retry behavior."}, {"question": "When should I keep the current setup?", "answer": "Keep or repair it when capture and destination acceptance meet the requirements and a replacement has not demonstrated a useful improvement."}];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/alternatives" class="link">← All alternatives</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Justuno alternatives: preserve capture before changing SMS</h1>
    <div class="prose-shopify mt-8">
      <h2>Start with the capture job</h2>
      <p>Justuno’s <a href="https://www.justuno.com/">current company site</a> describes popups, list growth and Spotlight visitor identification. Those can remain useful beside an existing sender. The <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/justuno-social-email-leads">Shopify listing retrieved on 25 November 2026</a> says the app is not currently available and directs support questions to Justuno. That listing status does not establish a company shutdown or the state of an existing account. Confirm installation and support options directly before making a replacement plan.</p>
      <h2>Retain, repair or replace the right layer</h2>
      <p>Keep Justuno if its capture experience and destination handoff meet your requirements. Repair a broken mapping or credential before replacing a working sender. For consolidation, ask your existing email/SMS supplier to demonstrate its own form against your actual capture requirements. A dedicated capture candidate must prove targeting, accessibility and field handling; an SMS candidate must separately prove sending, replies and destination support. Neither category automatically replaces the other. Adding Sequenzy solely because SMS changes has no established benefit here.</p>
      <h2>Proposed exercise: a skincare preference quiz</h2>
      <p>Use a controlled fixture, not live subscribers: a visitor selects skin preference, product interest and gift status, skips an optional age range, then chooses email only. Repeat with phone only and with no marketing permission. Justuno documents a <a href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/487-how-to-set-up-a-shopping-preference-quiz">shopping preference quiz</a>; this is a reason to preserve useful quiz behavior, not evidence that every candidate can reproduce it. Store the quiz version and answer keys so a renamed answer cannot silently change existing segments. These are proposed acceptance steps, not tests we performed.</p>
      <h2>Typed fields and identity acceptance</h2>
      <p>Create a mapping ledger with source field, destination attribute, type, allowed values and owner. Distinguish missing, empty, false and explicit deletion; a skipped age question must not overwrite a known value with zero. Preserve multiple selections without collapsing them into a string that downstream segments cannot use. Check international phone normalization, changed email addresses, returning anonymous visitors and shared devices. Define when records may merge, which identifier wins and how a mistaken merge is reversed. Visitor identification alone is not a new marketing opt-in.</p>
      <h2>A connector name is only the start</h2>
      <p>The <a href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/537-syncing-yotpo-to-justuno">Yotpo connector guide</a> describes passing new contacts and custom properties to a specified list. The <a href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/530-gdpr-justuno-consent-features">consent guide</a> warns that a provider may not track a checkbox choice through its standard integration. Demonstrate each intended connector and field combination in your account. Verify destination list, purpose, sender, disclosure version, timestamp and opt-in source; a successful API response is insufficient if the wrong list receives the record. Email-only choice must not enroll SMS.</p>
      <h2>Retries must preserve the visitor’s latest choice</h2>
      <p>Submit the same fixture twice, simulate a timeout after destination acceptance, then replay it after withdrawal. Require one intended enrollment, an inspectable failure queue and no permission resurrection. Give each submission a stable deduplication key and keep the original event time separate from retry time. Document rejection handling for invalid types and expired credentials. Reconcile counts of submitted, accepted, rejected and suppressed records with sample destination records; do not equate form submissions with reachable subscribers.</p>
      <h2>From capture to purchase without collisions</h2>
      <p>For a replenishment signup, gift buyer and opted-in VIP, inspect the actual destination journeys. A preference does not prove product usage timing. Choose timing and frequency from the promise made at signup and measured response, with local quiet-hour requirements reviewed for each SMS destination. At enrollment and send time, recheck purchase, withdrawal, stock and relevant support state. A completed checkout should cancel the applicable cart reminder without erasing unrelated education. Assign one owner per purpose and channel and a reply/STOP/HELP operator where SMS is used.</p>
      <h2>Cut over forms with a reversible boundary</h2>
      <p>Inventory embedded forms, mobile layouts, landing pages, checkout capture and cached scripts. Preserve exports, disclosure screenshots, mapping versions and restricted archive access before retiring anything. Stop old enrollments, reconcile pending destination jobs, and release one replacement capture path only after its records and suppressions reconcile. Late arrivals belong in a review queue rather than a second welcome journey. Rollback restores the known form and routing version while retaining new withdrawals; it must not replay every historical signup. Keep useful capture running if the proposed replacement cannot satisfy this boundary.</p>
      <h2>Compare ordinary and peak economics</h2>
      <p>Request matched quotes for the same eligible audience, destinations and sending volume. Include platform fees, connectors, implementation labor, SMS segments including Unicode, MMS and carrier charges where SMS is separately required. Push sends and SMS segments are different billing units. Record minimums, overages, registration, support and the cost of operating two systems. Compare refunds, opt-outs by flow, and repeat full-price purchases alongside attributed revenue; use a suitable holdout to estimate incremental orders.</p>
      <h2>Discounts need fixed-goods arithmetic</h2>
      <p>Illustrative assumptions, not merchant results: a $100 order with $45 goods cost and $10 other variable cost contributes $45 before messaging. A $25 discount leaves $20, keeping those costs fixed. Twenty incremental discounted orders contribute $400 before $300 campaign cost, leaving $100; thirty contribute $600 before $450 campaign cost, leaving $150. A discount alone does not prove a loss. Account for returns and purchases that would have happened anyway before claiming lift.</p>
      <p>Compare the separate handover in <a href="/alternatives/firepush-alternative">Firepush alternatives</a>: browser subscription continuity is different from capture-field acceptance.</p>
    </div>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Questions about Justuno alternatives" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
